# Thompson analysis for the section centralizer in 14.7.67(4)

The preparation constructs the genuine reduced internal module E in DR₁,
proves C_DR₁(E) = O₂(DR₁) = C_R₁(E), and constructs a faithful FF action
when D is not a two-group. It also proves non-two-groupness of J(DR₁)
and the returning-point core containment required by 14.7.31(2).

Final assembly remains here. The remaining component branch must prove
solvability of J(DR₁) using the full 14.3.4 and B.5.1 action conclusions.
The independent solvable branch must derive the S₃ quotient and apply
14.7.31 to the literal W₀(R₁,V), then rule out the nontrivial two-residual.
No final two-group assertion for D is claimed before both are discharged.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript, 1 March 2004,
proof of Lemma 14.7.67(4), printed pp.1070–1071, PDF pp.1087–1088.
-/
